  (b) modify the Software and create derivative works of it;
  (c) compile the Software and run the resulting binaries on any computer you
      own or control, for any purpose, including commercially, with no fee and
      no license key;
  (d) redistribute the Software in SOURCE form, modified or unmodified,
      including as a public fork or a contribution back to this project,
      provided a copy of this license is included and the notices in Section 4
      are preserved;
  (e) publish the results of any analysis of the Software — reviews, benchmarks,
      security findings, disassembly, teardowns — and quote from it as needed to
      support them, without restriction and without notice to the copyright
      holder.

2. CONDITIONS

You may not:

  (a) distribute the Software, or any derivative work of it, in BINARY or other
      non-source form, to anyone, whether or not for a fee;
  (b) remove, disable, or circumvent any license validation in the Software, or
      distribute anything designed to do so;
  (c) use the name "Cupertino", the bundle identifier `io.mgcrea.cupertino`, or
      the project's marks to identify a build you produced, in a way likely to
      suggest it is the official one.

Section 2(a) is the whole of the commercial reservation. A binary you compiled
for yourself under 1(c) is yours to run, on as many machines as you control, for
as long as you like. It is only handing that binary to someone else that is
reserved.

